  "id": "Compound::DB00263 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Sulfisoxazole may interact with Cyp2c9, through a shared structural similarity with sulfonamide antibiotics. This is supported by multiple paths indicating that Sulfisoxazole resembles sulfamoxole, sulfadimethoxine, and silver sulfadiazine, all of which are sulfonamide derivatives that bind to Cyp2c9. The low common ancestors of these compounds point to a common class of molecules—sulfonamide antibiotics—that share a structural profile likely involving a sulfonamide group. The final scores for all paths are consistent, indicating a robust and well-supported relationship between Sulfisoxazole and Cyp2c9, mediated through a shared pharmacophore or binding site. The evidence suggests that Sulfisoxazole may inhibit Cyp2c9 through a mechanism involving the sulfonamide group, which is a well-documented inhibitor of cytochrome P450 enzymes. This mechanism is further supported by the presence of multiple paths linking Sulfisoxazole to Cyp2c9, reinforcing the likelihood of a direct and mechanistically plausible interaction.",
